<!--
  T05 Collapse Policies

  ONE ROW PER TYPE FAMILY, EACH WITH THE POLICY THE SERVER ACCEPTS FOR IT:
  a date takes Latest, a counter takes Sum, a real takes Monotone, and a key
  or a flag takes none at all — and carries no unit, because neither is a
  quantity.

  A UNIT TEST DESIGN. Bundled with the app and read-only: suite [25]
  asserts what this file is supposed to prove, so editing it here
  changes what the harness tests.
-->
<gorp name="T05 Collapse Policies">
  <!-- nos-uml-state {"mode":"ai-design","title":"T05 Collapse Policies","layout":{"ut.collapse.Row":{"x":60,"y":60,"w":300,"h":220},"ut.collapse.Merge":{"x":440,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.collapse.Merged":{"x":800,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140}}} -->

  <comment view="class">One row per type family, each with the policy the server accepts for it. seen is a date and takes Latest; count is an integer and takes Sum; ratio is a real and takes Monotone; id is a key and ok is a flag, so neither takes a policy — and neither carries a unit, because neither is a quantity.

The rule is the server's, restated in Sai.CollapseRules: a measurement is for a quantity.</comment>
  <expect>Check finds nothing on any of the five rows.

Put a unit on id or on ok and Check must report "Measurement on a non-quantity". Drop the collapse from count or ratio and it must report the missing policy, naming the row.</expect>
  <model namespace="ut.collapse.Row">
    <variables>
      <variable name="id"    type="key" />
      <variable name="seen"  type="utcdatetime" collapse="Latest" />
      <variable name="count" type="int"    collapse="Sum"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="ratio" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="ok"    type="bool" />
    </variables>
  </model>

  <algorithm namespace="ut.collapse.Merge">
    <input  model="ut.collapse.Row" />
    <output model="ut.collapse.Merged" />
    <operations>
      <operation name="merge" returns="double" />
    </operations>
  </algorithm>

  <model namespace="ut.collapse.Merged">
    <variables>
      <variable name="total" type="int" collapse="Sum"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
    </variables>
  </model>
</gorp>
